# Tells GitHub Pages not to run Jekyll on this site.
#
# Jekyll ignores every directory whose name starts with an underscore, which
# would silently drop SvelteKit's _app/ directory -- so every stylesheet and
# script would 404 in production while working perfectly in local dev.
#
# The Actions-based deploy path (upload-pages-artifact + deploy-pages) does not
# run Jekyll, so this is belt-and-braces. It becomes load-bearing the moment
# anyone switches to deploying from a branch. It costs nothing, so keep it.
#
# Note: adapter-static does NOT create this file, despite what a lot of guides
# claim. Verified empirically -- it was absent from build/ until this file was
# added to static/.
